  "problem_statement": "Parser.named_fields returns incomplete list when field names contain hyphens\n\n#### Description\n\nWhen using field names with hyphens in parse templates, the `named_fields` property returns an incomplete list that's missing the last field name.\n\n#### Steps/Code to Reproduce\n\n```python\nimport parse\n\ntemplate = '/local/sub/{user-id}/duration'\nparser = parse.Parser(template)\nprint(\"Named fields:\", parser.named_fields)\nprint(\"Expected:\", ['user_id'])\n\n# Also affects templates with multiple hyphenated fields\ntemplate2 = '/foo/{user-id}/{user_id}/{user.id}/bar/'\nparser2 = parse.Parser(template2)\nprint(\"Named fields:\", parser2.named_fields)\nprint(\"Expected:\", ['user_id', 'user__id', 'user___id'])\n```\n\nThe `named_fields` property should return all field names but currently returns an incomplete list when hyphens are present in field names."
}